# Cross-engine comparison at 16 policies per arm, batched.
#
# The shape a real cluster runs: Kyverno's own Pod Security Standards CEL set
# ships 19 policies with no matchConditions and no selectors, so they all share
# one webhook and arrive in one call. The selectors variant reproduces that here;
# the matchconditions variant would instead give each policy its own endpoint and
# make every engine call carry exactly one policy.
#
# The minimal payload is deliberate. At the realistic payload the legacy kyverno
# arm saturates at 200 requests/s and its failures abort aggregation, which would
# cost all five arms. Use cel-ab-realistic-n16 and legacy-ab-realistic-n16 for
# realistic-payload work, one arm at a time.
ENGINES=${ENGINES:-"baseline kyverno kyverno-cel gatekeeper native"}
POLICY_COUNT=${POLICY_COUNT:-16}
KYVERNO_CEL_VARIANT=${KYVERNO_CEL_VARIANT:-selectors}
PAYLOAD_PROFILE=${PAYLOAD_PROFILE:-minimal}
TARGET_RPS=${TARGET_RPS:-200}
TRIALS=${TRIALS:-3}
PROFILE=${PROFILE:-scaling}
